The woman asks: "And your address?"
I say my address.
"I live at Solvej number seven," I say.
"On the second floor."
The woman listens and nods.
Then she writes it down.
She writes: "Solvej 7, 2. sal".
She looks at the paper and then at me.
She smiles.
"Good," she says.
It is official now.
Now the kommune knows where I live.
I have an address in Copenhagen.
It is a good feeling.
